{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00124",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.65,
      "end_seconds": 3.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Good morning. I hope the wait wasn't too long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.12,
      "end_seconds": 7.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. Thanks for seeing me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.95,
      "end_seconds": 13.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "You came on your own today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.6,
      "end_seconds": 17.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "I mean, yes, I managed on my own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.18,
      "end_seconds": 20.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Tell me what's been troubling you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.82,
      "end_seconds": 29.68,
      "duration_seconds": 7.86,
      "text": "Mainly I've been forgetting things lately. That's why I came. It's the not knowing that gets to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.05,
      "end_seconds": 33.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "How long has this been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.34,
      "end_seconds": 47.61,
      "duration_seconds": 13.27,
      "text": "Um, it's been nearly five years now. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest. I mean, I've been misplacing things too, for about a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.18,
      "end_seconds": 65.65,
      "duration_seconds": 16.47,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.23,
      "end_seconds": 68.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "Thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.51,
      "end_seconds": 71.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Any weakness on one side or headache?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.57,
      "end_seconds": 76.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "No weakness on one side or headache, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.21,
      "end_seconds": 81.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Bear with me, I need to finish this line in the notes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.77,
      "end_seconds": 94.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "Right, carry on. Alright, what about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.47,
      "end_seconds": 98.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "No, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.33,
      "end_seconds": 112.56,
      "duration_seconds": 12.23,
      "text": "It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.77,
      "end_seconds": 115.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "That's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.96,
      "end_seconds": 120.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.79,
      "end_seconds": 124.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Hmm, I've had high cholesterol, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.17,
      "end_seconds": 135.3,
      "duration_seconds": 9.13,
      "text": "Yes, I can see the high cholesterol in your file as well. Is it all right if a trainee sits in later? No? Fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.05,
      "end_seconds": 138.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "I'd rather not, if you don't mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.26,
      "end_seconds": 141.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "What medicines do you take regularly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.18,
      "end_seconds": 145.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "I'm on atorvastatin, 20 milligrams, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.52,
      "end_seconds": 149.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Do you have any questions before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.14,
      "end_seconds": 159.76,
      "duration_seconds": 9.62,
      "text": "Not at the moment, I think you've covered most of what I was wondering. If something comes to mind later, I'll ask you before I leave."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 160.53,
      "end_seconds": 168.27,
      "duration_seconds": 7.74,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Oxygen saturation is 97 percent, temperature is 37.0 degrees, BP is 113 over 70. Pulse 70."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.61,
      "end_seconds": 172.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Okay, noted. How's everything else at home otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.01,
      "end_seconds": 179.32,
      "duration_seconds": 5.31,
      "text": "Busy. Everyone's running in different directions at the moment, you know how it is."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.66,
      "end_seconds": 184.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.64,
      "end_seconds": 188.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Now I'm going to check this part."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.54,
      "end_seconds": 200.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Your gait is steady and the tone in your limbs is normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.0,
      "end_seconds": 220.93,
      "duration_seconds": 14.93,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Thank you for that. I'll write up what I found in a moment, and then I'll tell you what I think is going on. Has anything about your daily routine changed lately?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.39,
      "end_seconds": 239.38,
      "duration_seconds": 16.99,
      "text": "Okay, so not really, the days are pretty much the same, work and home, and I've been trying to fit appointments in around my schedule, which isn't always easy, so I'm glad we could find a time today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.9,
      "end_seconds": 252.02,
      "duration_seconds": 12.12,
      "text": "So, based on the history and the examination, my working impression is memory difficulties that need to be worked up. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 256.67,
      "end_seconds": 258.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Should I be worried about this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.13,
      "end_seconds": 281.69,
      "duration_seconds": 21.56,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's memory difficulties that need to be worked up, and we'll know more once the a CT scan of the head is back. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've been forgetting things lately for nearly five years, and no weakness on one side or headache."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 282.95,
      "end_seconds": 284.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.13,
      "end_seconds": 288.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "Is it okay if I type while we talk?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 290.06,
      "end_seconds": 293.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "Right, um, yes, of course, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.29,
      "end_seconds": 303.6,
      "duration_seconds": 9.31,
      "text": "I'm going to order a CT scan of the head, for memory loss. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 307.11,
      "end_seconds": 308.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Okay, um, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.19,
      "end_seconds": 330.64,
      "duration_seconds": 20.45,
      "text": "Keep a daily routine and write things down, a notebook by the door works well. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department. Please come and see me in four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 331.59,
      "end_seconds": 333.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "Well, okay, I'll book that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.24,
      "end_seconds": 341.04,
      "duration_seconds": 5.8,
      "text": "Tell me what you've taken from all that, so I can fill in any gaps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 342.19,
      "end_seconds": 347.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.42,
      "text": "So, um, I come back in four weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.94,
      "end_seconds": 355.09,
      "duration_seconds": 6.15,
      "text": "Alright, yes, exactly right. So, take care, and don't hesitate to call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 356.17,
      "end_seconds": 358.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "That's all, thank you for your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 360.3,
      "end_seconds": 361.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.07,
      "text": "See you then."
    }
  ]
}